    {
      "id": "claim_1f78622f04e04265b01f9678c67765d1",
      "statement": "A callback registered with CallbackRegistry (src/manifold/training/callbacks/registry.py) is a @dataclass whose fields are the config knobs and which exposes a build(ctx: CallbackContext) -> pl.Callback method. Specs match the CallbackSpec Protocol structurally (no inheritance); an optional logged_metrics: frozenset[str] declares metrics for monitor validation, and only CheckpointSpec declares monitor_metric. resolve() raises KeyError on an unknown name and ValueError on an unknown knob for a known name, using the field names of fields(spec_cls) as the knob allow-list.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/callbacks/registry.py",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:2c7eba43a15c1783f59d856a19ba24795a7ae3305b376368de28b760fceeb023"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/callbacks/registry.py#L73-L108",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4b2443053e896efe4a367a1e257a081625d88a47057e11c5419312bacb7dd091:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_db8e343916d24748aae82ebbe088a1dd",
      "statement": "CallbackRegistry construction is split into two phases: resolve(names, cfg) (config-time) validates the requested name list and per-name knob dict, returning constructed spec instances in names order; build(specs, ctx) (fit-prep) injects the runtime CallbackContext — module, vae, datamodule, inference_recipe, model_dir, seed, optional lazy feature_net_factory, optional real_latents — and returns the constructed pl.Callback list. The split exists because generative callbacks (FID, paired fidelity) need runtime objects unavailable at config resolution, and the resolved list is required to be rank-symmetric across DDP ranks.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/callbacks/context.py",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:4a4f9526087b7ba05a9f493a285cbd8a892439d7a8047e644b9a5029f2f2058b"
        },
        {
