    {
      "id": "claim_2f87ed820ff64aa59cd232a7ddd5868a",
      "statement": "PairedFidelitySpec (ADR-0037 / issue #238) is mounted on the supervised ControlNet path exactly like FIDSpec — knobs as dataclass fields, build(ctx) injecting module / vae / paired-subset source from ctx.datamodule, logged_metrics declared so validate_monitor accepts val/psnr and val/ssim as validatable monitors. The rollout step count is recipe-primary: num_inference_steps defaults to None and build reads it from ctx.inference_recipe[num_inference_steps] (the controlnet.num_inference_steps knob the supervised spine fills in), with an explicit per-callback knob overriding the recipe. The paired-subset source is resolved lazily at the first gated epoch (F5) via getattr(datamodule, \"val_latent_ds\", datamodule) so the cold path's post-setup() replacement is honored. Generation is gated by torch.inference_mode(), so the callback never enters the loss or touches the optimizer / EMA (observe-only contract).",
