    {
      "id": "claim_690eb1974df6472391798b36dd8db98b",
      "statement": "Adding a registry callback requires a @dataclass spec under src/manifold/training/callbacks/, exposure from src/manifold/training/callbacks/__init__.py, and a spine.registry.register(name, SpecCls) call in each CLI that wants it. Renaming a dataclass field is load-bearing: resolve then rejects any recipe that still uses the old name with a loud ValueError, which is the contract's signal that every recipe site needs an update. A new monitored metric must be declared as a spec's logged_metrics, the module's logged_metrics, or an extra_callbacks member's logged_metrics, otherwise validate_monitor rejects any checkpoint that monitors it. Dropping a callback for one policy should use forbidden_callbacks rather than hard-coding the absent name into default_names — the forbidden map is the post-merge, override-resistant path.",
      "evidence": [
